# Interests

Things I keep coming back to. Layperson enthusiasm in nearly all of these. Recommendations welcome!

## Writing & Language

* Creative nonfiction & literary journalism
* Poetry (Imagists, 20th-century American, poetry in translation)
* Learning French to read poetry untranslated
* WritePads & distraction-free digital typewriters
* Public domain work & remix culture
* Microessays, commonplace books, & zines

## The Small & Open Web

* The IndieWeb (POSSE, webmentions, owning your domain)
* Gemini, Gopher, Finger, & the oldnet/altnet
* The decentralized web (Mastodon, Bluesky, ATproto)
* Static site generators & progressive enhancement
* Accessibility-first design
* Digital third places & webmastering

## Technology & Tools

* Linux & ricing old ThinkPads (Debian-based, brutalist)
* Self-hosting & homelabs
* Mechanical keyboards
* Retro handheld gaming & itch.io indies
* Dumbphones, e-ink, & analog-leaning tech

## Thought & Study

* Religious studies (process theology, Mahayana Buddhism, Indigenous ways of knowing)
* Philosophy, Western & Eastern (absurdism, bioethics, free will)
* Cultural anthropology & the history of storytelling
* Independent academic research & open scholarship
* Mathematics & atmospheric oddities (sprites, elves, blue jets)
* Mycology, decomposition as creation

## Culture & Media

* Arthouse, indie, & Canadian cinema
* Animation (Adventure Time, BoJack, Smiling Friends)
* Fandom, fanfiction, & transformative works
* Coming-of-age & young adult narratives
* Music as memoir (Sufjan Stevens, Bon Iver, the Mountain Goats)
* Death culture & global rituals around mortality
* Public libraries & third places

## Living

* Bullet journaling & analogue systems (Traveler's notebooks, cheap coil pads)
* Walking & public transit
* Veganism & plant-based living
* Frugality & financial independence
* Self-quantification & meta-learning
* Slow living & intentional boredom

## Community & Change

* Activism, mutual aid, & pro bono work
* Progressive, communist, & anarchist politics
* Sustainability, ecology, & prairie landscapes
* Disability justice & chronic illness advocacy
* Decolonization & Métis identity

